  "result": "Two real transient acoustic cases with the same model, display mesh, volume mesh, boundary and 25 stored frames (source amplitudes 1 Pa and 2 Pa) produced an exact linear factor-of-two pressure response. GUI and official MCP produced byte-identical 5,574,849-byte GIFs with SHA-256 3c7ce9..., 24 full-canvas 640x320 frames, RGB332/256 colors, loop 0 and 8/9-centisecond delays summing to 200 centiseconds. A real browser ImageDecoder decoded all 24 frames with distinct pixel hashes. The manifest's common color range matches the actual stored-field min/max, the camera is fixed, interpolation is false, and only nearest stored frames are selected. Success and mid-run cancellation restored input, cases, result and comparison settings; cancellation refused the partial artifact. Stale revision, single time, reversed range and zero-tolerance unsaved time were rejected. No source or test change was needed.",
  "unconfirmed": [
    "The browser is the OpenCode desktop Electron/Chromium build, not branded Google Chrome.",
    "Only localhost was used; public HTTPS, OS download and cross-origin deployment were not verified.",
    "Only one acoustic model/mesh and one pair of source amplitudes were checked. There is no general acoustic-accuracy, convergence, mesh-independence or full-suite/post-push-CI claim.",
    "The GIF is lossy RGB332 with 256 colors; pixel hashes are over decoded RGB output, not a proof of pressure-value accuracy.",
    "The GIF is 5,574,849 bytes, above the 5 MiB single-file transfer limit. Full bytes were retrieved through 86 official MCP artifact pages; a direct one-file browser transfer was not used and is not claimed.",
    "GUI and MCP GIFs were byte-identical in this one run. No multi-run determinism distribution was measured.",
    "The saved case mesh has 2223 volume nodes while pressure arrays and the comparison range use 741 scalars per frame; the UI summary shows 741 nodes / 2672 tetrahedra. This distinction is recorded, not generalized.",
    "The static comparison-view preset remained 'Enter the shared physical time' because the time-video path used the explicit start/end fields; the preset and the video controls were both unchanged before/after.",
    "The parent VIEWCOMPARE unit remains incomplete; this is a bounded real-browser verification slice."
  ],
